    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0867" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg765"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.672/532b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the High Commissioner in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-04T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 4,
                                1927—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Treaty will be taken up in secret executive session of Senate today.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d716-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d716-f1" n="1" xml:id="d716-f1-content">
                <p>The general treaty between the United States and Turkey was signed at Lausanne,
                    Aug. 6, 1923 (<ref target="frus1923v02#pg_1153"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1923, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p.
                        1153</ref>). For previous correspondence concerning the ratification of the
                    treaty, see <ref target="frus1926v02#pg_974"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>,
                        1926, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 974</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
